            <ArticleTitle>Adult intussusception presenting with target sign.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1154-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1100/tsw.2008.150</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intussusception occurs when a proximal bowel segment telescopes into a contiguous distal portion. This report describes a rare case of idiopathic intussusception in a 48-year-old female, complaining of right-sided abdominal pain. The abdominal CT scan presents a classic target lesion, representing the cross-sectional image of the intussusceptum layers inside the outer intussuscipiens.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
